  "review_decisions": [
    "Reuse the existing Euclidean Schwartz transform and LCA Plancherel theorem rather than creating duplicate transform entries.",
    "Periodic elementary definitions expose the unit-cell and angular normalizations without requiring abstract representation theory.",
    "Angular averages specify cylindrical components, and product means state whether conjugation is present.",
    "Keep phase, amplitude, carrier parameter, wavevector, wavenumber, and wavelength as separately expandable concepts.",
    "Transversality cancels only the leading divergence term; the curl construction gives exact divergence freedom with an explicit correction.",
    "Pulse envelopes are pointwise amplitude bounds; derivative bounds and temporal zero extension are additional requirements.",
    "Reuse the existing moving-frame derivative formula, including its frame-motion term.",
    "Separate exact scalar damping factorization, envelope propagation, and Gaussian endpoint estimates.",
    "Derive affine-background plane-wave formulas directly; transversality gives exact self-interaction cancellation for these spatially constant amplitudes.",
    "Separate evaluation along a multivariable auxiliary map from the scalar phase in an oscillatory exponential; remove their ambiguous shared alias.",
    "Make nonzero carrier assumptions and complex cross-product conventions explicit."
  ],
